SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Damián Búho <damian.buho@proton.me>

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

Production JVM flags — flattened into JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS at startup.

AlwaysPreTouch:  touch all heap pages at startup to avoid page faults during
                 operation. Trades slower startup and higher RSS for
                 predictable latency.
DoEscapeAnalysis: JIT eliminates escape allocations on the stack.
ExplicitGCInvokesConcurrent: System.gc() triggers concurrent collection,
                             not a full STW pause.
OptimizeStringConcat: JIT optimises StringBuilder.append chains.
UseCompressedOops: use 32-bit compressed pointers (heap < 32 GB).
UseStringDeduplication: deduplicate String objects across the heap (ZGC-aware).
UseZGC: ZGC — low-latency, generational by default since JDK 21.
B19_JAVA_XMS / B19_JAVA_XMX: heap floor/ceiling, override per image.
#}

-XX:+AlwaysPreTouch
-XX:+DoEscapeAnalysis
-XX:+ExplicitGCInvokesConcurrent
-XX:+OptimizeStringConcat
-XX:+UseCompressedOops
-XX:+UseStringDeduplication
-XX:+UseZGC
-Xms{{ ENV.B19_JAVA_XMS }}
-Xmx{{ ENV.B19_JAVA_XMX }}
